# ---------- Data & model artefacts ----------
# Large CSVs are fetched, not committed (see README)
backend_house_prediction/data/*.csv

# The trained model IS committed (~1.5 MB), deliberately.
# The training CSV is too big for git, so the deploy host cannot retrain — it can
# only run what we ship. Leaving the artefact untracked meant Render served a
# stale model baked into a cached Docker layer, pickled by an older scikit-learn
# than the one requirements.txt installed, and the API died at startup.
# Committing it keeps the model and the code that loads it versioned together.
# Retrain + commit whenever the pinned scikit-learn version changes.
backend_house_prediction/models/*.joblib

